    <p class="tag">Specialised Service</p>
    <h1>ACR I-Card Assistance</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">Register, renew or replace your Alien Certificate of Registration I-Card without the guesswork.</p>

    <p>Most foreign nationals on a long-term visa in the Philippines, and tourist-visa holders who stay beyond a short-term period, are required to hold an Alien Certificate of Registration Identity Card (ACR I-Card). Foreign Immigration Services assists with registration, renewal and replacement.</p>

    <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Confirming whether your visa status requires an ACR I-Card</li>
      <li>Preparing and organising the required documentation</li>
      <li>Coordinating the registration, renewal or replacement process</li>
      <li>Keeping you informed as your application progresses</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Common Situations We Handle</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Registering for an ACR I-Card for the first time</li>
      <li>Renewing an ACR I-Card that is due to expire</li>
      <li>Replacing a lost, damaged or stolen ACR I-Card</li>
      <li>Confirming whether your specific visa status requires one</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How the Process Works</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Initial enquiry</h3>
        <p>Tell us your visa status and what you need help with.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Assessment</h3>
        <p>We confirm the requirements that apply to your specific situation.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Preparation</h3>
        <p>We help you prepare the documentation your application requires.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Submission and follow-up</h3>
        <p>We coordinate the application and keep you informed of its progress.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="context-note">
      <p>ACR I-Card requirements and validity depend on your specific visa category — we confirm exactly what applies to you as part of the assessment.</p>
    </div>

